  "live_records": {
    "q-13283": {
      "dom_id": "step-q13283",
      "name": "Question 1",
      "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14232805/assets/595066ea08080810e96c278b54c50f1da30eb155b2b36a29769591d89549a9fd.png)\n\nCalculate the volume of a cylinder given that its diameter is $34\\,\\text{m}$ and its height is $11\\,\\text{m}.$",
      "worked_solution": "The volume of a cylinder with radius $r$ and height $h$ is given by\n\n$$\nV=\\pi {r}^{2}h.\n$$\n\nSubstituting $r=\\frac{34}{2}=17\\,\\text{m}$ and $h=11\\,\\text{m}$ into the formula, we get\n\n$$\nV=\\pi (17)^{2}(11)=3\\,179\\pi \\,{\\text{m}}^{3}.\n$$",
