    "q-117870": {
      "dom_id": "step-q117870",
      "name": "Question 2",
      "problem": "Calculate the volume of a cylinder given that the circumference of the base is $14\\pi \\,\\text{m}$ and the ratio of its height to its radius is $\\frac{1}{49}.$",
      "worked_solution": "First, we find the radius $r$ using the formula $C=2\\pi r,$ where $C$ is the circumference, as follows: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}C & =2\\pi r \\\\ 14\\pi  & =2\\pi r \\\\ r & =7\\,\\text{m}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo find the height $h$, we use the fact that the ratio of the height to the radius is $\\frac{1}{49}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{h}{r} & =\\frac{1}{49} \\\\ \\frac{h}{7} & =\\frac{1}{49} \\\\ h & =\\frac{1}{7}\\,\\text{m}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe volume of a cylinder with radius $r$ and height $h$ is given by\n\n$$\nV=\\pi {r}^{2}h.\n$$\n\nSubstituting $r=7\\,\\text{m}$ and $h=\\frac{1}{7}\\,\\text{m}$ into the formula, we get\n\n$$\nV=\\pi \\cdot {7}^{2}\\cdot \\frac{1}{7}=7\\pi \\,{\\text{m}}^{3}.\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
        {
          "key": "selection",
          "type": "radio",
          "choices": [
