      "name": "Question 3",
      "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14232805/assets/68f26a479c5cc1efa978bf6a6390023c07b4215fd7d7d01eb834900d9be696cc.png)\n\nCalculate the volume of a cylinder given that its diameter is $10\\,\\text{in}$ and its height is $8\\,\\text{in}.$",
      "worked_solution": "The volume of a cylinder with radius $r$ and height $h$ is given by\n\n$$\nV=\\pi {r}^{2}h.\n$$\n\nSubstituting $r=\\frac{10}{2}=5\\,\\text{in}$ and $h=8\\,\\text{in}$ into the formula, we get\n\n$$\nV=\\pi (5)^{2}(8)=200\\pi \\,{\\text{in}}^{3}.\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
