    "q-13282": {
      "dom_id": "step-q13282",
      "name": "Question 4",
      "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14232805/assets/bc117c302bf4a2963dca000a030d92ae58e6dd13f236826505ca1e732015ba14.png)\n\nCalculate the volume of a cylinder given that its radius is $13\\,\\text{in}$ and its height is $19\\,\\text{in}.$",
      "worked_solution": "The volume of a cylinder with radius $r$ and height $h$ is given by\n\n$$\nV=\\pi {r}^{2}h.\n$$\n\nSubstituting $r=13\\,\\text{in}$ and $h=19\\,\\text{in}$ into the formula, we get\n\n$$\nV=\\pi (13)^{2}(19)=3\\,211\\pi {\\text{ in}}^{3}.\n$$",
