    "q-32475": {
      "dom_id": "step-q32475",
      "name": "Question 5",
      "problem": "Calculate the height $h$ of a cylinder given that its volume is $16\\pi \\,{\\text{cm}}^{3}$ and the ratio of its height to its radius is $2.$",
      "worked_solution": "Using the fact that  the ratio of the height $h$ to the radius of the base $r$ is $2,$ we have that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{h}{r} & =2 \\\\ r & =\\frac{h}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe volume of a cylinder with radius $r$ and height $h$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}V=\\pi {r}^{2}h.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting $V=16\\pi {\\text{ cm}}^{3}$ and $r=\\frac{h}{2}$ into the formula, we find the value of $h:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}V & =\\pi {r}^{2}h \\\\ 16\\pi  & =\\pi {(\\frac{h}{2})}^{2}\\cdot h \\\\ 16 & =\\frac{{h}^{3}}{4} \\\\ {h}^{3} & =64 \\\\ h & =4\\,\\text{cm}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
