    "q-32465": {
      "dom_id": "step-q32465",
      "name": "Question 6",
      "problem": "Calculate the circumference of the base of a cylinder given that its volume is $1\\,536\\pi \\,{\\text{cm}}^{3}$ and the ratio of its radius to its height is $\\frac{1}{3}.$",
      "worked_solution": "Using the fact that the ratio of the radius $r$ of the base to the height $h$ is $\\frac{1}{3},$ we have that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{r}{h} & =\\frac{1}{3} \\\\ h & =3r\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe volume of a cylinder with radius $r$ and height $h$ is given by\n\n$$\nV=\\pi {r}^{2}h.\n$$\n\nSubstituting $V=1\\,536\\pi \\,{\\text{cm}}^{3}$ and $h=3r$ into the formula, we can find the value of $r:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}V & =\\pi {r}^{2}h \\\\ 1\\,536\\pi  & =\\pi {r}^{2}(3r) \\\\ 1\\,536 & =3{r}^{3} \\\\ {r}^{3} & =512 \\\\ r & =\\sqrt[3]{512} \\\\ r & =8\\,\\text{cm}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the formula for the circumference of the base is $C=2\\pi r.$ So, we have\n\n$$\nC=16\\pi \\,\\text{cm}.\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
